elements inside of the curly braces when the condition changes. However, it has a
number of benefits:
 There are no imports, as we have seen.
 We can place multiple unrelated DOM elements inside the curly braces, while
NgIf only worked on a single element.
 It is more readable.
 There is no confusion as to where an if statement starts and ends
